  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic Investments Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Uganda):  The USAID-funded Feed the Future Strategic Investments Activity works to accelerate, catalyze, and unlock additional investment in the agriculture, productive use of energy, and health sectors. The Activity supports private sector enterprises to be investor-ready, secure loan guarantees to lower transaction costs and risks, and develop partnerships that unlock commercial investments. FY 2022 resources will fund transaction advisory services to at least 23 deals to make them investment ready.  FY 2022 funding will be used to provide advisory services, hold financing matchmaking events, conduct investment analyses, and design a virtual deal room to support pre-financial close negotiations between investors and investee projects in Uganda. FY 2022 funds will support private-sector-led innovation that increases the productive use of electricity by agricultural small- and medium-sized enterprises, farmer cooperatives, and farmers. The Activity will facilitate viable, commercially-driven local and international private sector investments that align with USAID&apos;s development objectives. For example, the majority of investments target the agricultural sector to increase agricultural production, improve food safety through post-harvest processing and storage, and increase the diversity of crops available to improve nutrition. Over its lifetime, the Activity will mobilize $140 million in private capital to Uganda while improving the livelihoods of 100,000 underrepresented and marginalized people.The Activity will contribute to the Gender Equity and Equality Action (GEEA) Fund priority 4: Promote entrepreneurship, and financial and digital inclusion, through investing in 12% women-owned enterprises, that together will seek $29 million in financing. The activity further will provide advisory services, facilitate access to relevant information  and engage women-led and -owned businesses who receive business development support...</narrative>
  </description>
